    "isHTML": true,
    "searchText": "Situation 3 \nJonnie an audit senior working on the audit of Big Corp plc (Big Corp). He is feeling a lot of \npressure to perform on the audit, as his father is the CFO of Big Corp. Jonnie has a challenging \nrelationship with his farther, and he doesn’t want his father to think that the audit is not \nprogressing because Jonnie isn’t competent. \nWhen working late one night Jonnie hears a disagreement between his audit partner, Lynn, and \nthe financial director (FD) of Big Corp. Lynn is complaining that Big Corp have not been making \npayments in line with the agreed fee schedule, and that there are now overdue audit fees of a \nsignificant value. The FD tells Lynn not to worry – the fees will be paid in the future, and as an \napology he will arrange dinner at a local fine-dining restaurant for Lynn and the audit team. ",
