    "isHTML": true,
    "searchText": "Situation 5 \nMel is an audit manager at L&J Limited, working on the audit of Wedding Accessories plc (WA), a \nlisted company. This year, Felix, who had previously been a payroll manager at WA, is joining the \naudit firm. Mel is considering including Felix in the audit team for the 20X4 audit of WA, as his \nknowledge of the client would be helpful. \nAs well as the statutory audit, L&J provides a variety of other non-audit services for WA.  In 20X4, \nthe audit fee is expected to be £200,000, and fees from non-audit services are expected to total \n£150,000, which is consistent with the last few years. \nOne service which L&J has been involved with is the design of the website (this does not include \nan e-commerce element). However there have been some serious security issues with this \nplatform which have caused significant financial losses, and WA are threatening to sue L&J for \nthe costs associated with these. \n ",
