    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/aa-ws1-acceptance-s2-q-1.png\" alt=\"Original workshop source extract\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/aa-ws1-acceptance-s2-a-1.png\" alt=\"Original workshop source extract\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "isHTML": true,
    "searchText": "Situation 2  \nRory is an audit partner at a small audit firm based in Inverness. He is preparing for the audit of \nScottie Shortbread Limited (Scottie). Scottie is usually one of his most straightforward clients as his \nwife is the CFO and they work well together.  \nThis year Rory and the other audit partners have been performing an analysis of the audit fees which \nthey receive from all their audit clients, and the resources required to complete the audit. Rory has \nnoticed that the audit fee for Scottie is 30% lower than average for a client of this size, however he \nknows that he will struggle to get his wife to agree to a higher fee. He has also realised that, due to \nthe acceptance of some other engagements, all associate staff members are fully resourced to the \naudits of other clients, and he does not yet have any assigned to Scottie. \n ",
