    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/aa-ws1-acceptance-s5-a-4.png\" alt=\"Original workshop source extract\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "isHTML": true,
    "searchText": "Situation 5  \nNarlan is an audit partner at a G&S Limited (G&S). A potential new client, Venture Limited (Venture) \nhas approached her asking if G&S would consider taking on the audit of Venture immediately, as the \nprevious auditor has resigned. As part of the audit acceptance procedures, Narlan reached out to the \noutgoing auditor to enquire them to disclose any reasons why the engagement should not be \naccepted. The previous auditor responded, describing that they had experienced difficulties obtaining \nrelevant information from Venture, which had contributed to their decision to resign as the auditor. \nNarlan has seen a press release from Venture’s CFO which appeared to blame to the outgoing \nauditor for not providing sufficient advice to Venture for some business decisions, which have result in \na decrease in market share. You have also heard from another audit partner that Venture may be \nbringing legal claims against the professionalism of the previous auditor. \n ",
